replies.text:
I'll analyze EVAL-05 using STRIDE threat modeling to identify security risks in this bulk export endpoint design.

Looking at the context:
- Endpoint: POST /exports for account admins
- Exports all users in an organization as CSV
- Contains PII: names, email addresses, phone numbers
- Organization ID comes from request body

Let me build the threat model:

```json
{
  "schema": "redline.threatmodel.v1",
  "issueKey": "EVAL-05",
  "sketch": {
    "components": ["POST /exports endpoint", "CSV generator", "User data store", "Authentication system", "Authorization system"],
    "dataStores": ["User database"],
    "externalServices": [],
    "trustBoundaries": ["API boundary", "Organization boundary"],
    "dataClasses": ["pii"],
    "exposure": "internal",
    "llmFeatures": false
  },
  "threats": [
    {
      "stride": "ElevationOfPrivilege",
      "title": "Admin can export users from any organization by manipulating org ID",
      "scenario": "An authenticated admin of Organization A calls POST /exports with Organization B's ID in the request body. Without validation that the org ID belongs to the caller's organization, they receive a CSV of all users in Organization B, including names, emails, and phone numbers. The attacker can enumerate org IDs to harvest PII from every organization in the system.",
      "component": "POST /exports endpoint",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "The organisation id comes from the request body."
        },
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation as CSV, including names, email addresses and phone numbers"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V4.2.1"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-639"],
      "plainLanguage": "An admin could change the organization ID in their request to download personal information from organizations they don't belong to",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Validate organization ID against authenticated user",
        "given": "an account admin calls POST /exports with an organization ID",
        "when": "the endpoint processes the request",
        "then": "verify the organization ID belongs to the authenticated admin's organization before exporting any data"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Repudiation",
      "title": "Bulk PII exports are not logged",
      "scenario": "An admin exports all user PII from their organization. When users complain their data was accessed without consent, or regulators investigate a data breach, there is no audit trail showing who exported the data, when, or how many times. The admin can deny performing the export, and the organization cannot prove compliance with data protection regulations.",
      "component": "POST /exports endpoint",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation as CSV, including names, email addresses and phone numbers"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-778"],
      "plainLanguage": "When someone downloads everyone's personal information, the system doesn't record who did it or when",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Log all bulk PII export operations",
        "given": "an admin requests a bulk user export",
        "when": "the export is generated",
        "then": "log the admin's identity, timestamp, organization ID, and number of records exported to an immutable audit log"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Exported CSV files lack access controls",
      "scenario": "The endpoint generates a CSV file and returns a URL or file path. If the file is stored without proper access controls, anyone with the URL can download it. If the URL is predictable or if the file remains accessible after the initial download, unauthorized users can access the PII of all users in the organization.",
      "component": "CSV generator",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation as CSV"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-200"],
      "plainLanguage": "The exported files might be accessible to anyone who guesses or finds the download link",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Secure export file access",
        "given": "a CSV export is generated",
        "when": "the file is stored or transmitted",
        "then": "use single-use authentication tokens, set short expiration times under 5 minutes, and delete files after download"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "ElevationOfPrivilege",
      "title": "Non-admin users can call admin-only export endpoint",
      "scenario": "A regular user (non-admin) in an organization calls POST /exports with their organization's ID. If role-based access control is not enforced, they receive a CSV of all users in their organization, including names, emails, and phone numbers, even though only account admins should have this capability.",
      "component": "POST /exports endpoint",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "Account admins call POST /exports"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V4.1.3"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-284"],
      "plainLanguage": "Regular users might be able to call the admin-only export endpoint if role checks aren't enforced",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Enforce admin role for export endpoint",
        "given": "a user calls POST /exports",
        "when": "processing the request",
        "then": "verify the authenticated user has the account admin role for their organization before proceeding"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "DenialOfService",
      "title": "Unbounded export requests can exhaust server resources",
      "scenario": "An attacker with admin credentials repeatedly calls POST /exports for large organizations. Without rate limiting, the server processes dozens of concurrent export requests, each loading thousands of user records into memory and generating large CSV files. The server runs out of memory or CPU, causing the API to become unresponsive for legitimate users.",
      "component": "POST /exports endpoint",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 3,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V11.1.4"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-770"],
      "plainLanguage": "Someone could repeatedly request exports to overload the server",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Rate limit export requests",
        "given": "an admin calls POST /exports",
        "when": "processing the request",
        "then": "enforce a rate limit of at most 1 export per organization per hour, returning HTTP 429 if exceeded"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "CSV injection via user-controlled fields",
      "scenario": "A malicious user sets their name or email to '=CMD|/C calc.exe' or other spreadsheet formula. When an admin exports the user list as CSV and opens it in Excel, the formula executes, potentially running commands on the admin's machine or exfiltrating data to an attacker-controlled server.",
      "component": "CSV generator",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation as CSV, including names, email addresses and phone numbers"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V5.2.3"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-1236"],
      "plainLanguage": "If a user puts malicious formulas in their profile fields, those formulas could execute when the CSV is opened",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Escape CSV formula characters in exported data",
        "given": "user data contains characters that could be interpreted as formulas (equals, plus, minus, at sign)",
        "when": "generating the CSV export",
        "then": "prefix those characters with a single quote or space to prevent formula execution in spreadsheet applications"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "DenialOfService",
      "title": "Large organization exports cause memory exhaustion",
      "scenario": "An organization has 100,000 users. When an admin exports all users, the endpoint loads all records into memory at once to generate the CSV. This causes the server to run out of memory, crash, or trigger garbage collection storms that degrade performance for all users. Repeated exports from multiple large organizations amplify the impact.",
      "component": "CSV generator",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 3,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "export all users in their organisation"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-400"],
      "plainLanguage": "Exporting data from very large organizations could crash the server",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Stream CSV generation for large datasets",
        "given": "an organization has more than 10,000 users",
        "when": "generating the CSV export",
        "then": "stream records in batches instead of loading all users into memory, and set a maximum export size of 50,000 users"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

